From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 21:52:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] plat-ls: seed core ASLR from TF-A's SEC RNG

CFG_CORE_ASLR is on by default, but on Layerscape it randomized nothing.
The seed comes from a /secure-chosen/kaslr-seed property in the device
tree the previous stage passes, and failing that from
plat_get_aslr_seed(). NXP's TF-A passes BL32_FDT_OVERLAY_ADDR, where no
device tree has been written when OP-TEE starts, and plat-ls had no
plat_get_aslr_seed(), so the weak default returned 0 and the core was
mapped at the same address on every boot of every part.

NXP's TF-A already serves random numbers from the SEC (CAAM) RNG through
the SiP call 0xC200FF11 -- U-Boot uses it to give Linux its kaslr-seed --
and BL31 brings the SEC up before it enters BL32, with its runtime
services registered by then. Ask it for eight bytes. It is the one
hardware RNG reachable this early; OP-TEE's own CAAM driver starts long
after the core is mapped, and the Cortex-A72 has no RNDR.

If the call fails, log it and map the core at its fixed address rather
than stopping the boot.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
---
 core/arch/arm/plat-ls/main.c | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/arch/arm/plat-ls/main.c b/core/arch/arm/plat-ls/main.c
index 51e5d46a1..654ef5842 100644
--- a/core/arch/arm/plat-ls/main.c
+++ b/core/arch/arm/plat-ls/main.c
@@ -328,3 +328,31 @@ bool plat_rpmb_key_is_ready(void)
  */
 #error "CFG_RPMB_WRITE_KEY needs SFP_BASE and SNVS_BASE for this flavour"
 #endif /* SFP_BASE && SNVS_BASE && CFG_RPMB_FS */
+
+#ifdef CFG_CORE_ASLR
+/*
+ * NXP's TF-A serves random numbers from the SEC (CAAM) RNG through a SiP
+ * call, and BL31 has the SEC running before it enters OP-TEE. That is the one
+ * hardware RNG reachable this early: OP-TEE's own CAAM driver starts long
+ * after the core is mapped. A failed call leaves the core at its fixed
+ * address rather than stopping the boot.
+ */
+#define NXP_SIP_RNG_64		0xC200FF11
+
+unsigned long plat_get_aslr_seed(void)
+{
+	struct thread_smc_args args = {
+		.a0 = NXP_SIP_RNG_64,
+		.a1 = 1,	/* eight bytes rather than four */
+	};
+
+	thread_smccc(&args);
+	if (args.a0 || !args.a1) {
+		EMSG("No ASLR seed from TF-A (%#"PRIx64"), core mapped at its fixed address",
+		     args.a0);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
+	return args.a1;
+}
+#endif /* CFG_CORE_ASLR */
-- 
